  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Twende Mbele (meaning &#x201c;going forward together&#x201d;) is a program of the University of the Witwatersrand, in Johannesburg, South Africa, that connects African government officials to strengthen the use of evidence in public decision&#x2011;making and support regional peer&#x2011;learning, benchmarking, and knowledge&#x2011;sharing activities to improve government monitoring, evaluation, and service delivery outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
